From 8c278b913cd1acf5c76a401a9c753ca0c5c0f153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ch0mpaa <christian.gonzalez@infosystemsinc.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen27 CUDA: prompt cache with resumable prefill and a pinned
 host-memory tier

Keeps and resumes prompt states for the qwen27 CUDA engine. A state is a stream's DeltaNet recurrences and
conv windows plus the first N rows of each attention layer's keys and values. A pass with the cache in play
cuts the zero-anchored chunk grid, so kept states line up across requests, and keeps the prompt matmuls for
every piece, so resumed passes compute the same tokens as cold ones. TF_QWEN27_HOST_CACHE_GIB=N keeps the
states in N GiB of pinned host memory instead of the card's spare memory, which lets a 262K window cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
